      {
        "question": "What is the difference between rock-on-rock and rock-on-anvil VSI crushers?",
        "answer": "A rock-on-rock VSI uses a bed of material as part of the impact zone, while a rock-on-anvil VSI directs accelerated material against stationary wear-resistant anvils. The appropriate configuration depends on the feed material, abrasiveness, production requirements and desired product."
      }
